  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.5.0: Task-based API; no Azure Quantum SDK dependency\n- BREAKING: every solver, builder, ML and algorithm entry point is `xAsync … cancellationToken : Task<…>`; the synchronous and Async<_> variants and all [<Obsolete>] wrappers are gone. Migrate `X.solve …` → `X.solveAsync … CancellationToken.None`; in a script finish with `|> Async.AwaitTask |> Async.RunSynchronously`\n- BREAKING: every computation expression (`binaryClassification`, `optionPricing`, `chemistry`, …) returns Task<QuantumResult<_>>; the C# builders expose only `…Async(…, CancellationToken)`\n- BREAKING (workspace): AzureQuantumWorkspace reads quotas and provider status from the REST data plane; Microsoft.Azure.Quantum.Client and Azure.Quantum.Jobs are no longer referenced. WorkspaceConfig gains HttpClient (and createWithHttpClient); InnerWorkspace is gone\n- CHANGED (cloud fan-out): kernel matrices, SVM evaluation, VQC and Primitives.sampleBatchAsync/observeBatchAsync keep at most JobThrottle.MaxConcurrentSampledJobs (8) circuits in flight on a sampling backend; error-mitigation noise levels and benchmark suites run one after another\n- CHANGED: cancellation surfaces as OperationCanceledException instead of an Error; Knapsack's classical fallback no longer runs after the caller cancelled\n- CHANGED (bin packing): the bin bound is the first-fit-decreasing count, not the item count, so a 6-item problem that fits 2 bins takes 14 qubits instead of 42\n- CHANGED (cost dashboard): \"today\" and \"this month\" buckets use the local calendar instead of UTC\n- ADDED (LocalQuantumService): GET {workspace}/quotas and GET {workspace}/providerStatus, so the workspace client runs offline too\n- FIXED (tests): the QuantumClient facts returned Async<unit> and were never run by xUnit; they run now",
